  body: "# Overlapping benefits in DMG chapter 17\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe chapter addresses duplication
    of payment where entitlement to more than one relevant benefit or dependency increase exists, and distinguishes
    incompatible benefits.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nEntitlement to both benefits is different from both being
    payable in full. Public-funds restrictions, exceptions, dependency increases and international provisions require
    their own review. No award calculation or assumption that all benefits overlap is made.\n\n## Inspected source
    passages\n\n- [DMG 17001, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n- [DMG 17004, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n- [DMG 17005, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/62d7b8d5d3bf7f2865c6fe43/dmgch17.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 17: Overlapping benefits.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of
    the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance,
    not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file
    positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve
    extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability
    remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch17` PDF SHA-256: `ce6967960168b301ae0b454df6824017202f6d3f6a14282a7ef0d4778bdac19a`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `c00f0acadb11047d22fe6c046a756a164cc7be254aaebfb91470f2f38201af99`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-incompatible-benefits
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly distinguishes overlap from cases where entitlement to one benefit
      prevents entitlement to another.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch17/0002
      quote: "17005 - and those not payable out of public funds - see DMG 17006.\n\n\nIncompatible benefits\n17005
        Benefits can only overlap where there is entitlement to both or all of those benefits. There can be\nno
        overlap where entitlement to one benefit is prevented by entitlement to another benefit. These\nbenefits
        are referred to as being incompatible. See Appendix 1 for a list of incompatible benefits."
      locator: DMG 17005
